<title>USA: Ryland stake raised by Tweedy Browne group.</title>
<headline>Ryland stake raised by Tweedy Browne group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Tweedy Browne Co LP, a New York-based broker-dealer, said Tuesday it raised its stake in Ryland Group Inc to 1,074,745 common shares or 6.84 percent from 5.76 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 105,685 common shares bought between Sept 6 and Oct 31 at prices ranging from $13 to $14.375 per share.</p>
<p>The group holds the stake for investment purposes, the filing said.  Ryland is a Columbia, Md.,-based homebuilder and mortgage financing company.</p>
</text>
